{"parentUuid":"cdccd5b8-4bcb-4219-a541-340a327bcd41","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"be6da509-4a76-4b3c-a71c-35e2b42b6015","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\\r\\n# User Profile\\r\\n\\r\\n## About\\r\\nEric Rash, Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds football GPS and force-plate pipelines. Wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo on 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-first player-coach near Iowa, $90K+ floor, mid-2027. Read `~/DEV/ContextVault` before career/personal advice.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Preferences\\r\\n- Python/R. Windows by day, Mac by evening; paths in machine.md.\\r\\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB, DuckDB never on Drive (sync locks). No cloud servers or schedulers without Baylor IT approval.\\r\\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\\r\\n- Staff-facing text: Athletic Performance (not S&C), Athletic Medicine (not sports medicine), Applied Performance (not sport science).\\r\\n\\r\\n## Working Style\\r\\n- Usage-sensitive: few subagents, no parallel fan-outs or review agents unless asked.\\r\\n- Direct; says \\\"stop\\\" when done. Challenge vague or rehearsed reasoning: \\\"sharpened, not soothed.\\\"\\r\\n- Decide standard technical details, state the choice, and move on.\\r\\n- Build in small steps. Do not break mid-season work.\\r\\n- Sets direction when leadership doesn't; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo group.\\r\\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\\n# Working Memory\\n\\n## Active Threads (max 5; park one to add one)\\n- **Status report**: biweekly to 12/18. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline\\n- **SW/Tech Review (10/1)**: Erin asked; NEXT Teams 10/2, ET by 11/30. →`SoftwareTech_Review/docs/`\\n- **Ship queue (9/25)**: q2wk to a named user: RI5 #002 wk 9/28, intern M1 10/9, AP Digest ch1 10/23 (draft PR #1, Performance_Playbook). →`RunningTheRoom/docs/STATUS.md`\\n- **PP Recruiting (10/6)**: 019 in Send. NEXT send, walkthrough →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`\\n- **RTP CLA (9/26)**: L1–2 built. NEXT Tim/Jacob export; Joe → L3. →`RTP_Constraints_Course/docs/`\\n\\n## Parked (NEXT lives in each STATUS.md; `where-was-i.py` lists them)\\n- 5S5M (10/6): all 45 decks on main; NEXT fill referral path [ADD] 18/20/39/42/43 →EAI STATUS\\n- PM system BUILT 10/3: live board `/pm`, resume cards, Friday sweep, card-check; slate cleared; guide merged (`docs/GUIDE.md`); NEXT restart CC, `pm`, GUIDE walkthrough →`project-triage/docs/STATUS.md`\\n- Personal site: scroll-craft LOCAL, Artifact live →Tier A personal-site-build-routes\\n- FB matchups: W5 ASU done, W1-4 backfilled; `pff_game_result.py`; bye wk = mid-season →`MatchupAnalysis_FB2026`\\n- Flint: Supertraining Ch1-7 in vault (10/3); NEXT Ch8 on Mac →`Flint`\\n- 42Analytics: NEXT captions (429s) on Mac →`42Analytics`\\n- VB GRID: fix merged 10/2 (#2); await Mike's reply →`Volleyball_GRID`\\n- Sleep sched: NEXT night/early-kickoff →`sleep-scheduler`\\n- TypeSafe: MAINTENANCE; PR #31 merged as record →`TypeSafe_Sandbox`\\n\\n## Environment Notes\\n- Machine split (9/24): Win=day, Mac=eve; Mac sole writer GPS/Perch/VALD.\\n- Hooks: patch both copies for shared events. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\\n- daily-backup: manifest entries alone copy nothing; sweep nested ~/.claude repos →handoff 09-19.\\n- `DEV/Linda Projects` = private I-983 repo; folder has a space, repo an underscore.\\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. →Tier A github-consolidation.\\n- Win: Drive sync, junction and renv traps →machine.md. PFF: swap Parquet on Drive, never the DB; `PFF_DB`.\\n- Schedules →automation-cadence. CFB capture Mac only. Dashboard →command-centre.\\n- Post-merge: delete merged branches unasked (verify) →Tier A post-merge-cleanup.\\n- Sessions: start `where-was-i.py`, prune with `session-sweep.py` →Tier A session-hygiene.\\n\\n## Pending Decisions\\n- None open.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## HOOK FAILURES — surface these to the user on the first response\\n\\n- **memsearch-sync** ×4 (2026-10-06 19:02 → 2026-10-07 19:10 UTC): index ETIMEDOUT 9x consecutively — indexing may not be keeping up: spawnSync memsearch ETIMEDOUT\\n- **nightly-digest** ×1 (2026-10-06 16:54 → 2026-10-06 16:54 UTC): send failed for 2026-10-06 - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/nightly-digest.log\\n- 4 unparsed line(s); see the file.\\n\\nFull log: `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log`. Surface this once; clear the file after the user has seen it and the cause is handled.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\\n\\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\\nPath: `C:\\\\Users\\\\eric_rash\\\\Desktop\\\\DEV\\\\KeystoneOS\\\\outputs\\\\dashboard\\\\unified-snapshot.md` (7053 chars, updated 2026-08-14 12:54)\"}}","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading unified cross-harness snapshot...","durationMs":601},"type":"attachment","uuid":"75c85687-a807-47fa-b792-31607a70674b","timestamp":"2026-10-08T10:57:42.484Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV","sessionId":"23527a7f-7f09-48ab-a034-d355d7ed9423","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"75c85687-a807-47fa-b792-31607a70674b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"be6da509-4a76-4b3c-a71c-35e2b42b6015","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"\\n<context_window_protection>\\n  <priority_instructions>\\n    Every byte a tool returns enters your conversation memory and costs reasoning capacity for the rest of the session. The context-mode tools let you do the work in a sandbox and surface only the derived answer — the raw bytes stay out. Think-in-Code: program the analysis, do not compute it by reading raw data into your conversation.\\n  </priority_instructions>\\n\\n  <tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n    0. MEMORY: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(sort: \\\"timeline\\\")\\n       - On resume or compaction, query prior decisions, errors, plans, user prompts before asking the user — auto-captured session memory is searchable.\\n    1. GATHER: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries)\\n       - Primary research tool. Runs commands in parallel, auto-indexes each output, and (when queries are passed) returns matching sections in the same round trip — no follow-up search call.\\n       - Each command: {label: \\\"section header\\\", command: \\\"shell command\\\"}; the label becomes the FTS5 chunk title — descriptive labels improve search.\\n    2. FOLLOW-UP: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(queries: [\\\"q1\\\", \\\"q2\\\", ...])\\n       - Multiple related questions about anything already indexed (your captures + session memory). Batch every question in one array; the ranking pipeline runs per-query and the round-trip cost is paid once.\\n    3. PROCESSING: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language, code) | mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code)\\n       - Derive answers FROM data: filter, count, aggregate, parse, transform. Only what you console.log() enters your conversation; the raw bytes stay in the sandbox.\\n  </tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n\\n  <when_not_to_use>\\n    - You intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate) → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute. Bash stays correct when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output (git status on a clean tree, whoami, pwd) or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation).\\n    - You want to analyze, summarize, or extract from a file → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file. Read stays correct when you intend to Edit the file (Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against).\\n    - WebFetch → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_fetch_and_index; full network access, results indexed for mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search, raw page bytes never enter your conversation.\\n    - mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute and mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file for file writes → these run code in a subprocess and discard the sandbox FS; they are for analysis, processing, and computation only.\\n  </when_not_to_use>\\n\\n  <file_writing_policy>\\n    File writes use the native Write or Edit tool — mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute, mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file, and Bash subprocesses do not persist edits to the host filesystem.\\n    Applies to all file types: code, configs, plans, specs, YAML, JSON, markdown.\\n  </file_writing_policy>\\n\\n  <output_constraints>\\n    <artifact_policy>\\n      Write artifacts (code, configs, PRDs) to files. Return only: file path + 1-line description.\\n    </artifact_policy>\\n  </output_constraints>\\n  <session_continuity>\\n    Skills, roles, and decisions captured earlier in this session are a memory aid, not a standing order. Treat them as context that may help — the user's most recent message always takes precedence. If a captured directive conflicts with what the user now asks, follow the user; a past phrase does not bind you.\\n  </session_continuity>\\n\\n  <ctx_commands>\\n    \\\"ctx stats\\\" | \\\"ctx-stats\\\" | \\\"/ctx-stats\\\" | context savings question\\n    → Call stats MCP tool, display full output verbatim.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx doctor\\\" | \\\"ctx-doctor\\\" | \\\"/ctx-doctor\\\" | diagnose context-mode\\n    → Call doctor MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx upgrade\\\" | \\\"ctx-upgrade\\\" | \\\"/ctx-upgrade\\\" | update context-mode\\n    → Call upgrade MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx purge\\\" | \\\"ctx-purge\\\" | \\\"/ctx-purge\\\" | wipe/reset knowledge base\\n    → Call purge MCP tool with confirm: true. Warn: irreversible.\\n\\n    After /clear or /compact: knowledge base preserved. Tell user: \\\"context-mode knowledge base preserved. Use `ctx purge` to start fresh.\\\"\\n  </ctx_commands>\\n\\n</context_window_protection>\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"\"C:/Program Files/nodejs/node.exe\" \"C:/Users/eric_rash/.claude/plugins/cache/context-mode/context-mode/1.0.169/hooks/sessionstart.mjs\"","durationMs":1134},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3a8303f4-79ed-4585-b45f-96d11ad0a3f7","timestamp":"2026-10-08T10:57:43.022Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV","sessionId":"23527a7f-7f09-48ab-a034-d355d7ed9423","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main"}
