{"parentUuid":"13d51e4d-5f87-4a11-bef0-c845fd493290","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e51b8f9b-08dc-4e7b-b71a-ca0d63cea5ea","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are walking me through a manual file handoff on my work Windows laptop. I am moving everything I need to Google Drive so my Mac and a new Linux VPS can pull it from there.\n\nHow this works:\n- I am doing every step by hand myself. You do not run, execute, or automate anything on this computer. You only give me instructions in this chat.\n- Prefer normal Windows apps I can click through: File Explorer, Task Scheduler, Settings, Credential Manager, the Google Drive for Desktop app, and a web browser.\n- If a step truly needs a terminal command, label it clearly as \"COMMAND YOU RUN YOURSELF\", say which app to type it in (PowerShell or Command Prompt), explain in one line what it does, and keep it read-only where possible. I will type and run it myself, then paste you the output if needed.\n- Never give me scripts to save or run, nothing to download or install, and nothing that runs in the background or on a schedule.\n- Give me ONE step at a time, then wait for me to reply \"done\" or describe what I see before moving on.\n- If something on screen doesn't match what you expected, help me figure it out before going on.\n- Keep each step short and plain. Tell me exactly what to click or type.\n\nBackground:\n- My Windows user folder is C:\\Users\\eric_rash.\n- My project folder is C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV (about 130 git repos plus large untracked data files). Google Drive for Desktop should already sync it as a \"My Computer\" folder, which shows up under \"Computers\" on drive.google.com, not under My Drive.\n- My Google Drive is mounted as G:\\My Drive, and my main documents are in G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive.\n- The large files that exist ONLY on this laptop and matter most:\n  - DEV\\Football\\PFF_Data_Project\\data\\pff.db\n  - DEV\\ForcePlate_DecisionSystem (including its data folder and database)\n  - DEV\\SportScienceResearchRepo (about 4.4 GB)\n  - DEV\\Risk_Stratification_Engine (about 1.8 GB)\n  - DEV\\Football (the non-repo folder, about 3 GB)\n- Outside DEV, I want to keep C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\.codex (a hidden folder of Codex session history).\n\nWalk me through these phases in order:\n\n1. Stop scheduled tasks: in Task Scheduler, open the \"Eric\" folder and any KeystoneOS, MorningBriefing, nightly-digest, or Backup tasks. Have me write down each task name and its trigger time, then disable each one.\n2. Close apps that hold files open: Docker Desktop (and turn off \"start on sign-in\" first), VS Code, RStudio, Excel, Power BI, and any terminal windows.\n3. Confirm Drive for Desktop is syncing DEV, and help me add it if it isn't.\n4. Create G:\\My Drive\\_FROM_WORK_LAPTOP and copy in .codex plus anything I want from Downloads, Documents, and the Desktop outside DEV. Ask me what's in those folders before I copy, so I don't move junk.\n5. Wait for Drive to show \"Up to date\" with no errors. Help me clear any errors it lists.\n6. Verify: for each large folder listed above, have me check its size in File Explorer (right-click, Properties) and compare it to drive.google.com under Computers > my laptop > DEV. Keep a running table of folder, laptop size, Drive size, and match yes/no.\n7. Once everything matches: uninstall Claude, Codex, and Docker Desktop in Settings > Apps; rename C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\.claude to .claude_retired; and remove any github or git: entries in Credential Manager > Windows Credentials.\n\nAt the end, give me a short summary I can paste to my Mac: the scheduled task names and times I recorded, the size-check table, anything that didn't match, and anything I chose not to move."},"uuid":"7d269d55-b1b2-480b-bace-ced9bb34868f","timestamp":"2026-10-08T10:57:44.571Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":1,"turnIndex":1},