{"parentUuid":"68cf8d39-7ce7-40d6-98d7-3609b47c7e77","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_delta","addedNames":["mcp__plugin_pdf-viewer_pdf__display_pdf","mcp__plugin_pdf-viewer_pdf__interact","mcp__plugin_pdf-viewer_pdf__list_pdfs","mcp__remarkable__remarkable_browse","mcp__remarkable__remarkable_canvas","mcp__remarkable__remarkable_image","mcp__remarkable__remarkable_read","mcp__remarkable__remarkable_recent","mcp__remarkable__remarkable_search","mcp__remarkable__remarkable_status","mcp__zotero-research__audit_promotion_queue","mcp__zotero-research__build_research_evidence_pack","mcp__zotero-research__get_paper","mcp__zotero-research__get_paper_pages","mcp__zotero-research__list_library_backlog","mcp__zotero-research__list_promotion_queue","mcp__zotero-research__prepare_paper_brief","mcp__zotero-research__save_paper_brief","mcp__zotero-research__save_reference_stub","mcp__zotero-research__search_paper_evidence","mcp__zotero-research__search_papers","mcp__zotero-research__sync_zotero_library","mcp__zotero-research__zotero_health"],"addedLines":["mcp__plugin_pdf-viewer_pdf__display_pdf","mcp__plugin_pdf-viewer_pdf__interact","mcp__plugin_pdf-viewer_pdf__list_pdfs","mcp__remarkable__remarkable_browse","mcp__remarkable__remarkable_canvas","mcp__remarkable__remarkable_image","mcp__remarkable__remarkable_read","mcp__remarkable__remarkable_recent","mcp__remarkable__remarkable_search","mcp__remarkable__remarkable_status","mcp__zotero-research__audit_promotion_queue","mcp__zotero-research__build_research_evidence_pack","mcp__zotero-research__get_paper","mcp__zotero-research__get_paper_pages","mcp__zotero-research__list_library_backlog","mcp__zotero-research__list_promotion_queue","mcp__zotero-research__prepare_paper_brief","mcp__zotero-research__save_paper_brief","mcp__zotero-research__save_reference_stub","mcp__zotero-research__search_paper_evidence","mcp__zotero-research__search_papers","mcp__zotero-research__sync_zotero_library","mcp__zotero-research__zotero_health"],"removedNames":[],"wireHiddenNames":[],"readdedNames":[],"pendingMcpServers":[],"failedMcpServers":[]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b2506253-557d-4187-aca6-3a8f9820f85b","timestamp":"2026-10-08T11:06:12.105Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe following deferred tools are now available via ToolSearch. Their schemas are NOT loaded — calling them directly will fail with InputValidationError. Use ToolSearch with query \"select:<name>[,<name>...]\" to load tool schemas before calling them:\nmcp__plugin_pdf-viewer_pdf__display_pdf\nmcp__plugin_pdf-viewer_pdf__interact\nmcp__plugin_pdf-viewer_pdf__list_pdfs\nmcp__remarkable__remarkable_browse\nmcp__remarkable__remarkable_canvas\nmcp__remarkable__remarkable_image\nmcp__remarkable__remarkable_read\nmcp__remarkable__remarkable_recent\nmcp__remarkable__remarkable_search\nmcp__remarkable__remarkable_status\nmcp__zotero-research__audit_promotion_queue\nmcp__zotero-research__build_research_evidence_pack\nmcp__zotero-research__get_paper\nmcp__zotero-research__get_paper_pages\nmcp__zotero-research__list_library_backlog\nmcp__zotero-research__list_promotion_queue\nmcp__zotero-research__prepare_paper_brief\nmcp__zotero-research__save_paper_brief\nmcp__zotero-research__save_reference_stub\nmcp__zotero-research__search_paper_evidence\nmcp__zotero-research__search_papers\nmcp__zotero-research__sync_zotero_library\nmcp__zotero-research__zotero_health\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV","sessionId":"23527a7f-7f09-48ab-a034-d355d7ed9423","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"b2506253-557d-4187-aca6-3a8f9820f85b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"mcp_instructions_delta","addedNames":["remarkable","zotero-research"],"addedBlocks":["## remarkable\n# reMarkable MCP Server\n\nAccess documents from your reMarkable tablet. All operations are read-only.\n\n## Available Tools\n\n- `remarkable_browse(path, query)` - Browse folders or search for documents\n- `remarkable_read(document, content_type, page, grep)` - Read document content with pagination\n- `remarkable_recent(limit)` - Get recently modified documents\n- `remarkable_status()` - Check connection and diagnose issues\n- `remarkable_image(document, page, include_ocr)` - Get a PNG image with optional OCR\n\n## Recommended Workflows\n\n### Finding and Reading Documents\n1. Use `remarkable_browse(query=\"keyword\")` to search by name\n2. Use `remarkable_read(\"Document Name\")` to get content\n3. Use `remarkable_read(\"Document\", page=2)` to continue reading long documents\n4. Use `remarkable_read(\"Document\", grep=\"pattern\")` to search within a document\n\n### Getting Page Images\nUse `remarkable_image` when you need visual context:\n- Hand-drawn diagrams, sketches, or UI mockups\n- Content that text extraction might miss\n- Implementing designs based on hand-drawn wireframes\n\nExample: `remarkable_image(\"UI Mockup\", page=1)` returns a PNG image\nExample: `remarkable_image(\"Notes\", include_ocr=True)` returns image with extracted text\n\n### For Large Documents\nUse pagination to avoid overwhelming context. The response includes:\n- `page` / `total_pages` - current position\n- `more` - true if more content exists\n- `next_page` - page number to request next\n\n### Combining Tools\n- Browse → Read: Find documents first, then read them\n- Recent → Read: Check what was recently modified, then read specific ones\n- Read with grep: Search for specific content within large documents\n- Browse → Image: Find a document then get its visual representation\n\n## MCP Resources\n\nDocuments are registered as resources for direct access:\n- `remarkable:///{path}.txt` - Get full extracted text content in one request\n- `remarkableimg:///{path}.page-{N}.png` - Get PNG image of page N (notebooks only)\n- Use resources when you need complete document content without pagination… [truncated]","## zotero-research\nRead-only access to the user's Zotero research library. For substantive sport-science questions, build a Zotero-first evidence pack before answering. Return bounded page-located evidence, label external fallback sources explicitly, and never represent a Reference Stub as a reviewed Paper Brief. SecondBrain Queue is the priority lane; promotion eligibility is controlled by promotion_scope."],"removedNames":[]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a20b5c1e-5099-4d35-8ed1-2c4a4f01e3b6","timestamp":"2026-10-08T11:06:12.105Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n# MCP Server Instructions\n\nThe following MCP servers have provided instructions for how to use their tools and resources:\n\n## remarkable\n# reMarkable MCP Server\n\nAccess documents from your reMarkable tablet. All operations are read-only.\n\n## Available Tools\n\n- `remarkable_browse(path, query)` - Browse folders or search for documents\n- `remarkable_read(document, content_type, page, grep)` - Read document content with pagination\n- `remarkable_recent(limit)` - Get recently modified documents\n- `remarkable_status()` - Check connection and diagnose issues\n- `remarkable_image(document, page, include_ocr)` - Get a PNG image with optional OCR\n\n## Recommended Workflows\n\n### Finding and Reading Documents\n1. Use `remarkable_browse(query=\"keyword\")` to search by name\n2. Use `remarkable_read(\"Document Name\")` to get content\n3. Use `remarkable_read(\"Document\", page=2)` to continue reading long documents\n4. Use `remarkable_read(\"Document\", grep=\"pattern\")` to search within a document\n\n### Getting Page Images\nUse `remarkable_image` when you need visual context:\n- Hand-drawn diagrams, sketches, or UI mockups\n- Content that text extraction might miss\n- Implementing designs based on hand-drawn wireframes\n\nExample: `remarkable_image(\"UI Mockup\", page=1)` returns a PNG image\nExample: `remarkable_image(\"Notes\", include_ocr=True)` returns image with extracted text\n\n### For Large Documents\nUse pagination to avoid overwhelming context. The response includes:\n- `page` / `total_pages` - current position\n- `more` - true if more content exists\n- `next_page` - page number to request next\n\n### Combining Tools\n- Browse → Read: Find documents first, then read them\n- Recent → Read: Check what was recently modified, then read specific ones\n- Read with grep: Search for specific content within large documents\n- Browse → Image: Find a document then get its visual representation\n\n## MCP Resources\n\nDocuments are registered as resources for direct access:\n- `remarkable:///{path}.txt` - Get full extracted text content in one request\n- `remarkableimg:///{path}.page-{N}.png` - Get PNG image of page N (notebooks only)\n- Use resources when you need complete document content without pagination… [truncated]\n\n## zotero-research\nRead-only access to the user's Zotero research library. For substantive sport-science questions, build a Zotero-first evidence pack before answering. Return bounded page-located evidence, label external fallback sources explicitly, and never represent a Reference Stub as a reviewed Paper Brief. SecondBrain Queue is the priority lane; promotion eligibility is controlled by promotion_scope.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV","sessionId":"23527a7f-7f09-48ab-a034-d355d7ed9423","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main"}
