{"parentUuid":"1a8fe7a1-adea-4d54-b85b-04cd75482de5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpfM9QYhs43KiDERopvG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can see 5 tasks in the \"Eric\" folder. Here's the record so far:\n\n| # | Task name | Trigger | Last run result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Backup AI Sessions to Drive | 12:30 AM every day | **0x1 (failed)** |\n| 2 | claude-files-digest | 6:30 AM every day | OK |\n| 3 | memsearch-drain-nightly | 9:00 PM every day | **0x1 (failed)** |\n| 4 | memsearch-drain-weekly | 2:00 AM every Sunday | OK |\n| 5 | nightly-digest | 9:00 PM every day | OK |\n\nThe backup task failed last night, so don't count on it having copied anything recent. The manual copy in Phase 4 covers that.\n\n## Phase 1, Step 2: Disable all 5 tasks\n\nFor each of the 5 tasks:\n\n1. Click the task in the list.\n2. In the right pane under **Selected Item**, click **Disable**.\n3. Its **Status** column should change from **Ready** to **Disabled**.\n\nLeave the **GoogleSystem**, **Microsoft**, and **SoftLanding** folders alone. Those belong to Google and Windows.\n\nReply \"done\" when all 5 show **Disabled**. In the next step we'll check the main library for KeystoneOS or MorningBriefing tasks stored outside the Eric folder.\n\nneeds input: Disable the 5 tasks in the Eric folder and reply \"done\" once each one shows Disabled."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6444,"cache_read_input_tokens":77419,"output_tokens":735,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":227},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6444,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":735,"cache_read_input_tokens":77419,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6444,"ca