{"parentUuid":"2c0e76b0-76ee-4232-9864-74a38dfe8b06","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpfT9pHDq7NY28CCphae","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":125,"cache_read_input_tokens":84598,"output_tokens":950,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":304},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":125,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":950,"cache_read_input_tokens":84598,"cache_creation_input_tokens":125,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":125},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3112,"serverClassifierRequest":"959eb2c1-e5b8-4780-9f0c-2107842a2042","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfpfT9Rhx5ZNX75PLFzTi","type":"assistant","uuid":"9e97708a-ad8b-4721-b2cb-e9e40671cee1","timestamp":"2026-10-08T11:07:40.561Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"23527a7f-7f09-48ab-a034-d355d7ed9423","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV","sessionId":"23527a7f-7f09-48ab-a034-d355d7ed9423","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"9e97708a-ad8b-4721-b2cb-e9e40671cee1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpfT9pHDq7NY28CCphae","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes. Each task is just a schedule plus one command it runs. The schedule is easy to recreate anywhere. What matters is whether the script it runs works on the other machine.\n\n- **On the Mac:** macOS uses launchd instead of Task Scheduler, and your stack already runs launchd jobs there. Some of these 5 may already have Mac versions. We'll check that on the Mac later, not here.\n- **On the VPS:** Linux uses cron or systemd timers for the same thing. The scripts would need Linux paths, and anything Windows-only (PowerShell, `G:\\` paths) would need rewriting.\n- **One thing to check for the VPS:** your profile notes say no cloud servers or schedulers without Baylor IT approval. Personal jobs are fine. Anything touching Baylor data (memsearch over work notes, digests of work sessions) should get that approval before it runs there.\n\nTo make porting easy, save each task's full definition before you disable it. Task Scheduler can export a task to a small text file (XML) that lists its exact command, arguments, and schedule. This only saves a copy; it doesn't change or run anything.\n\n## Phase 1, Step 2 (updated): Export, then disable\n\nFirst, create the folder **G:\\My Drive\\_FROM_WORK_LAPTOP\\scheduled-tasks** in File Explorer. We'll reuse `_FROM_WORK_LAPTOP` in Phase 4.\n\nThen, for each of the 5 tasks:\n\n1. Click the task.\n2. In the right pane, click **Export...**, save it into that `scheduled-tasks` folder, and keep the default file name.\n3. Click **Disable**. The Status should change to **Disabled**.\n\nReply \"done\" when all 5 are exported and show **Disabled**.\n\nneeds input: Export each of the 5 tasks to G:\\My Drive\\_FROM_WORK_LAPTOP\\scheduled-tasks, disable all 5, then reply \"done\"."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":125,"cache_read_input_tokens":84598,"output_tokens":950,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":304},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":125,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":950,"cache_read_input_tokens":84598,"cache_creation_input_tokens":125,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":125},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"959eb2c1-e5b8-4780-9f0c-2107842a2042","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfpfT9Rhx5ZNX75PLFzTi","type":"assistant","uuid":"58475001-20a0-43c7-8a58-3f86f7bc83ce","timestamp":"2026-10-08T11:07:46.566Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"23527a7f-7f09-48ab-a034-d355d7ed9423","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV","sessionId":"23527a7f-7f09-48ab-a034-d355d7ed9423","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main"}
