{"parentUuid":"c45e6d4f-91f7-41a7-8761-8fd3116fe42f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpgPuFhqiRbXX9kdw3x7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Docker's start-on-sign-in setting is now off. The box is unchecked and **Apply** is greyed out, so the change saved. But the bottom-left of your screenshot still says **Engine running**. If you already quit after taking it, you're fine. If not, right-click the whale in the tray, choose **Quit Docker Desktop**, and wait for the icon to disappear.\n\nDocker is using 14 GB of disk, mostly the Milvus search index for memsearch. That index is rebuilt from your notes, so you don't need to move it. I'll list it under \"chose not to move\" in the summary.\n\n## Phase 2, Step 2: Close the other apps\n\nClose each of these if it's open. Save any work first.\n\n1. **VS Code**: File > Exit.\n2. **RStudio**: File > Quit Session. If it asks to save the workspace, choose **Don't Save** unless you need it.\n3. **Excel**: close all workbooks.\n4. **Power BI Desktop**: close it.\n5. **Terminals**: close every PowerShell, Command Prompt, Windows Terminal, and Git Bash window.\n\nLeave **this Claude window** and **Google Drive for Desktop** open. You need both for the next phases.\n\nWhen you're done, check the system tray once more. You should see no whale icon and no VS Code or RStudio icons.\n\nneeds input: Confirm Docker has quit, close VS Code, RStudio, Excel, Power BI and all terminals, then reply \"done\"."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1682,"cache_read_input_tokens":93482,"output_tokens":695,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":213},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1682,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{