{"parentUuid":"5fccfefb-352c-46ae-ada2-97ac12944a41","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpgTMvenZnWeCFk1cQgS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":229,"cache_read_input_tokens":96191,"output_tokens":893,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":419},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":229,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":96191,"cache_creation_input_tokens":229,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":229},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":4521,"serverClassifierRequest":"9fa07c7e-b263-436f-814c-2fb75707beb8","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfpgTMb4b8eFjDjskU72n","type":"assistant","uuid":"7b0aaea3-f165-43d4-ac92-e195820e0a67","timestamp":"2026-10-08T11:20:49.612Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"23527a7f-7f09-48ab-a034-d355d7ed9423","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV","sessionId":"23527a7f-7f09-48ab-a034-d355d7ed9423","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"7b0aaea3-f165-43d4-ac92-e195820e0a67","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpgTMvenZnWeCFk1cQgS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes. The index isn't original data. memsearch builds it by reading your markdown files: memory files, daily logs, and the compiled knowledge articles. Any machine that has those files can build its own index. Your Mac most likely already has one, since memsearch runs there too.\n\nThe catch is the **source files**, not the index. Some of them may exist only on this laptop:\n\n- **Windows-only project memory.** Memory saved here goes to folders like `~/.claude/projects/C--Users-eric-rash-Desktop-DEV/memory/`. The Mac uses different folder names, so those files aren't automatically on the Mac.\n- **Anything in `~/.claude` that never got pushed to GitHub**, such as recent daily logs or memory edits.\n\nYour plan only copies `.codex` and renames `.claude` to `.claude_retired`. I'd add one item to Phase 4: copy the memory folders out of `.claude` into `_FROM_WORK_LAPTOP`. They're small text files, so it costs almost nothing, and the Mac or VPS can rebuild its index from them. I'll ask you about this when we get to Phase 4.\n\nIf you ever rebuild the index by hand, don't just run `memsearch index`. It can wipe the existing index. I'll put that warning in the Mac summary.\n\nBack to Phase 2:\n\nneeds input: Close VS Code, RStudio, Excel, Power BI and all terminal windows, then reply \"done\"."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":229,"cache_read_input_tokens":96191,"output_tokens":893,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":419},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":229,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tok