{"parentUuid":"049d6941-aaca-4301-af14-ed055413d984","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfph3hsun4EtDAEhTCVbf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That clears up the errors. None of them explain the missing 2.8 GB:\n\n| Error | What it is | Action |\n|---|---|---|\n| `_DRIVE` | Junction to your whole Drive | Expected. Ignore it. |\n| `ZoteroInjestion` | Junction | Expected. Ignore it. |\n| `S064.gdoc` | A tiny shortcut file that points to a Google Doc. The real document is already in Google Docs, and Drive never uploads these shortcuts. | Harmless. Ignore it. |\n\nSo the gap needs a closer look. Drive's 12.8 GB figure may just be an estimate, or it may be measured differently. The way to settle it is to compare folders directly, which is what Phase 6 does. For that I need a reliable way to see sizes on the Drive side, and your G: drive may provide one.\n\n## Phase 3, Step 5: Look for \"Other computers\" on G:\n\n1. In File Explorer, type `G:\\` in the address bar and press Enter.\n2. Tell me which folders you see. I'm hoping for one called **Other computers** or **Computers**.\n3. If it's there, open it and tell me what's inside. Look for a laptop name, then **DEV** under it.\n\nIf this view exists, you can right-click folders there and get the size Drive actually stored. That makes Phase 6 a straight side-by-side comparison.\n\nneeds input: Open G:\\ in File Explorer and tell me what folders are listed, especially whether \"Other computers\" exists."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":837,"cache_read_input_tokens":105128,"output_tokens":1181,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":689},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":837,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","i