{"parentUuid":"e3e30b70-20f1-4b32-9814-ed973bf43460","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfq94CXcSmtneriQjEqoi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"On Drive, **pff.db is 524 KB, last changed Sep 22.** That's small for a full PFF database. Your recollection points the right way: my notes say \"swap Parquet on Drive, never the DB\" and mention a `PFF_DB` setting. That suggests:\n\n- The **real database lives somewhere other than this folder**. A `PFF_DB` environment variable tells your scripts where it is.\n- **Drive only gets the small Parquet snapshots.** The two `video_*.parquet` files dated Oct 3 match that.\n- Your notes also say the **Mac is the only machine that writes GPS, Perch, and VALD data**. Whether that includes PFF, I'm not sure.\n\nSo yes, the real data may already live on the Mac or somewhere else, and this `pff.db` may be an old stub. Two checks will tell us.\n\n## Phase 3, Step 10: Compare the laptop copy and find PFF_DB\n\n**Check A, laptop size:**\nIn File Explorer, go to `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Football\\PFF_Data_Project\\data`, right-click **pff.db**, choose **Properties**, and note the **Size** and **Modified** date.\n\n**Check B, where PFF_DB points:**\n1. Click **Start**, type **environment variables**, and open **Edit environment variables for your account**.\n2. In the top list (User variables), look for **PFF_DB** and note its value.\n\nSend me both. If the laptop copy is also 524 KB and PFF_DB points elsewhere, we'll add that location to the checklist.\n\nneeds input: Send the size and modified date of DEV\\Football\\PFF_Data_Project\\data\\pff.db on the laptop, and the value of the PFF_DB environment variable (or tell me it isn't there)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":93692,"cache_read_input_tokens":32373,"output_tokens":998,"output_tokens_details":