{"parentUuid":"d91ab057-77bc-49fe-9480-2e769a8774ee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfq9ttTnPGFc94yaLfFoG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"There's a lot in your user folder: about 95 dot-folders from various AI tools and CLIs, dot-files like `.gitconfig`, `.bashrc`, `.zshrc` and `.claude.json`, and several regular folders that look like your own data. Since you want everything, let's measure before copying. Some dot-folders can be huge and are just rebuildable caches, especially `.ollama` (local AI models), `.cache`, `.docker` and `.vscode` (extensions).\n\nRegular folders that look like they could hold data that exists only here:\n\n- **Zotero**: possibly your Zotero library and attached PDFs\n- **SECRETS_QUARANTINE**\n- **DEV_archive_hold**, **drive_reorg_logs**, **odysseus**, **printing-press**, **go**, **bin**, **Evernote**\n- **Documents**, **Downloads**, **Desktop** (outside DEV), **Pictures**, **Videos**\n\nWe'll handle those after the dot-folders.\n\n## Phase 4, Step 3: Measure all the dot-folders together\n\n1. Click **.adal** (the first folder in the list).\n2. Scroll to **.zencoder** (the last dot-folder, in the middle column), hold **Shift**, and click it. Every dot-folder should now be highlighted.\n3. Right-click any highlighted folder and choose **Properties**.\n4. Wait for the **Size** to stop climbing, then tell me the Size and the Contains line.\n\nIf the total is under about 10 GB, we'll copy all of them as-is. If it's much bigger, we'll find the one or two heavy folders and decide on those.\n\nneeds input: Select .adal through .zencoder, open Properties, and send the total Size and Contains once it stops changing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2315,"cache_read_input_tokens":133577,"output_tokens":1356,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":778},"server_tool