{"parentUuid":"4d4f3787-ef00-47e8-8c2b-2b410829abe6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqA3vSqbWNSwoPxK5QW5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":437,"cache_read_input_tokens":137248,"output_tokens":753,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":338},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":437,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":753,"cache_read_input_tokens":137248,"cache_creation_input_tokens":437,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":437},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3270,"serverClassifierRequest":"33da6b6c-b34a-4e5c-b754-213cbeddac9f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfqA3uv6MULghjUJrr5xc","type":"assistant","uuid":"881288c4-0f59-48b5-95de-021b02a8acf0","timestamp":"2026-10-08T17:22:41.379Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"23527a7f-7f09-48ab-a034-d355d7ed9423","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV","sessionId":"23527a7f-7f09-48ab-a034-d355d7ed9423","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"881288c4-0f59-48b5-95de-021b02a8acf0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqA3vSqbWNSwoPxK5QW5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dot-folders add up to **24.9 GB across about 216,000 files.** The file count is the bigger problem. Drive uploads many small files very slowly, often only a few per second, so 216,000 files could take a day or more. Most of that bulk is probably in a handful of folders.\n\n## Phase 4, Step 4: Find the heavy folders\n\nCheck **Properties > Size** on each of these one at a time, and send me the list of sizes:\n\n1. `.ollama`: local AI models, usually several GB each\n2. `.cache`: download caches for various tools\n3. `.claude`\n4. `.codex`\n5. `.vscode`: editor extensions\n6. `.docker`\n7. `.local`: uv, Python tools\n8. `.memsearch`\n9. `.cursor`\n\nThen I'll suggest a split. Your own data (`.claude`, `.codex`, `.ssh`, configs) gets copied as-is. Rebuildable bulk, like models, caches, and extensions, either gets skipped or packed into a single zip file, which Drive uploads far faster than thousands of loose files. You decide which.\n\nneeds input: Send the Properties Size for .ollama, .cache, .claude, .codex, .vscode, .docker, .local, .memsearch and .cursor."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":437,"cache_read_input_tokens":137248,"output_tokens":753,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":338},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":437,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":753,"cache_read_input_tokens":137248,"cache_creation_input_tokens":437,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":437},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit