{"parentUuid":"caa2a45e-c6cc-4272-942f-c631e860037e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqAboaEkra5X5J4cnA33","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":127,"cache_read_input_tokens":143286,"output_tokens":1075,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":578},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":127,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1075,"cache_read_input_tokens":143286,"cache_creation_input_tokens":127,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":127},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":5964,"serverClassifierRequest":"27f07922-f2b1-4848-8440-4d71a8a42ef4","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfqAbnpMjxeX5aN1NowR4","type":"assistant","uuid":"61c19310-7d95-4e69-a9fc-45140a3feb18","timestamp":"2026-10-08T17:29:56.596Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"23527a7f-7f09-48ab-a034-d355d7ed9423","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV","sessionId":"23527a7f-7f09-48ab-a034-d355d7ed9423","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"61c19310-7d95-4e69-a9fc-45140a3feb18","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqAboaEkra5X5J4cnA33","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Use **separate zips, one per folder.** Three reasons:\n\n- **If one fails, you only redo that one.** Windows' built-in zip can stop on a single locked file or an overly long path. With one big zip, a failure at 20 GB means starting over.\n- **Easier sorting on the Mac.** You can unpack `claude.zip` today and leave `vscode.zip` alone until you need it, or never.\n- **Smaller uploads.** If Drive stalls, you can see which file it's stuck on.\n\nThe plan:\n\n| Zip | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| claude.zip | .claude |\n| codex.zip | .codex |\n| vscode.zip | .vscode |\n| cache.zip | .cache |\n| local.zip | .local |\n| memsearch.zip | .memsearch |\n| dotfolders-other.zip | All the other ~85 dot-folders together |\n| (no zip) | Loose dot-files like `.gitconfig` and `.bashrc`, copied as-is |\n\nExplorer builds each zip next to the original folder on C:, and then we move it to G:. That temporarily needs up to about 25 GB of free space on C:, so check that first.\n\n## Phase 4, Step 5: Check free space on C:\n\n1. In File Explorer's left pane, click **This PC**.\n2. Under **Devices and drives**, look at **Windows (C:)** and tell me the \"**X GB free of Y GB**\" line.\n\nneeds input: Tell me how much free space Windows (C:) shows under This PC."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":127,"cache_read_input_tokens":143286,"output_tokens":1075,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":578},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":127,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1075,"cache_read_input_tokens":14