{"parentUuid":"266f6c0d-6db3-4863-a3e4-520b89c3c8cd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqAih1YNeFduL7c965mt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39,"cache_read_input_tokens":144488,"output_tokens":715,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":342},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":715,"cache_read_input_tokens":144488,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3864,"serverClassifierRequest":"3609f999-444b-4df9-a4bb-6b9a17666453","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfqAigcF32jB5fFAAf1c8","type":"assistant","uuid":"1c1d7084-bef0-4649-937d-9cf26d1c2ccd","timestamp":"2026-10-08T17:31:27.943Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"23527a7f-7f09-48ab-a034-d355d7ed9423","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV","sessionId":"23527a7f-7f09-48ab-a034-d355d7ed9423","version":"2.1.294","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"1c1d7084-bef0-4649-937d-9cf26d1c2ccd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqAih1YNeFduL7c965mt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes. Your Windows build has the newer zip tool, which can save a zip to a different location. Right-click a folder, choose **Compress to > Additional options**, and you'll get a box where you choose where the zip goes. So you can write straight to **CRASHBOX (D:)** and leave C: alone. You also end up with a second copy on a drive you hold in your hand.\n\nThere's one thing to check first. Some external drives are formatted as **FAT32**, which can't hold any file larger than 4 GB. `vscode.zip` and `claude.zip` could both go over that, and the zip would fail partway through.\n\n## Phase 4, Step 5 (updated): Check CRASHBOX\n\n1. In File Explorer, click **This PC**.\n2. Right-click **CRASHBOX (D:)** and choose **Properties**.\n3. Tell me:\n   - **File system**: NTFS, exFAT, or FAT32\n   - **Free space**\n\nIf it's NTFS or exFAT with at least about 30 GB free, we'll zip to D:.\n\nneeds input: Send the File system and Free space shown in CRASHBOX (D:) Properties."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39,"cache_read_input_tokens":144488,"output_tokens":715,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":342},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":715,"cache_read_input_tokens":144488,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"3