{"parentUuid":"e5a9c926-a6b6-4281-a81c-222209b23cd4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqAnBxAnUEJ9GzmTzPeq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"CRASHBOX is **NTFS with 1.12 TB free**, so there's plenty of room and no 4 GB file limit. We'll zip straight to D:.\n\nQuick question while you work: is CRASHBOX a **physical external drive you'll keep**? It holds 2.51 TB of data. If it's actually a second disk *inside* this laptop, that data leaves with the laptop, and we need to plan for it.\n\n## Phase 4, Step 6: Make the first zip (.codex)\n\nWe'll start with `.codex` and do `.claude` last. This Claude session is still writing into `.claude`, so it should be zipped as late as possible.\n\n1. Make sure the **Codex** app is closed.\n2. In File Explorer, go to `D:\\`, right-click an empty spot, choose **New > Folder**, and name it `_FROM_WORK_LAPTOP`.\n3. Go to `C:\\Users\\eric_rash`, right-click **.codex**, and choose **Compress to > Additional options**.\n4. In the box that opens:\n   - **Destination / location:** browse to `D:\\_FROM_WORK_LAPTOP`.\n   - **File name:** `codex.zip`\n   - **Archive format:** ZIP\n   - Leave the other settings at their defaults.\n5. Click **Create**, then wait for it to finish. 3.3 GB may take a few minutes.\n\nIf the box looks different from this, send me a screenshot before clicking Create. If an error comes up partway, send a screenshot of it.\n\nneeds input: Zip .codex to D:\\_FROM_WORK_LAPTOP\\codex.zip, then reply \"done\" with the zip's size (or a screenshot of any error). Also tell me whether CRASHBOX is a drive you'll keep."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":451,"cache_read_input_tokens":145242,"output_tokens":1043,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":462},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","ca