{"parentUuid":"6903e114-730b-4e93-9dd6-144a0de086f8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqBRDBcwuZBF4Z8jyPHA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That's almost certainly the **ChatGPT desktop app running in the background**. Codex is part of ChatGPT now, so even with no window open, a background process can hold `.codex` files open. Let's close it properly, then redo the zip.\n\n## Phase 4, Step 7: Fully quit ChatGPT, then retry\n\n1. If the error box is still open, click **Cancel**. Don't click \"Skip\", or the zip will be missing that file.\n2. Check the **system tray** (click the **^** by the clock). If there's a ChatGPT icon, right-click it and choose **Quit**.\n3. Press **Ctrl + Shift + Esc** to open **Task Manager**. On the **Processes** tab, look for anything named **ChatGPT** or **Codex**. Click each one and then **End task**.\n4. In `D:\\_FROM_WORK_LAPTOP`, delete the partial **codex.zip** if one is there.\n5. Redo the `.codex` zip the same way as before.\n\nIf the error comes back, send me a screenshot that shows the **file name** it complains about.\n\nAlso: did the **vscode** zip (or any other one running at the same time) hit an error, or is it still going?\n\nneeds input: Quit ChatGPT fully (tray + Task Manager), delete the partial codex.zip, retry the .codex zip, and tell me the result."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":128,"cache_read_input_tokens":147848,"output_tokens":615,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":174},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":128,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":615,"cache_read_input_tokens":147848,"cache_creation_input_tokens":128,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_inp