{"parentUuid":"0ad940b2-ec02-43aa-85c8-af1d53d6672b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqBdu4os53ieeEcYhRzo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This one is different. **codex.exe is running right now**, and it's what holds the lock. The lock file itself is empty, but while codex.exe runs, it may be writing to Codex's real database in the same folder. Zipping that mid-write can produce a damaged copy. Stop codex.exe and start this zip over.\n\nThe Codex plugin in this Claude session may have started codex.exe in the background. Ending it doesn't affect anything we're doing.\n\n1. Click **Cancel**.\n2. Open **Task Manager** (**Ctrl + Shift + Esc**) and click the **Details** tab on the left. It lists every program by its .exe name.\n3. Click the **Name** column to sort, then find every **codex.exe** and **ChatGPT.exe**. Right-click each one and choose **End task** (or **End process tree**).\n4. Delete the partial **codex.zip** in `D:\\_FROM_WORK_LAPTOP`.\n5. Redo the `.codex` zip.\n\nThis time you should get no \"in use\" errors, or at most the 0-byte `.guard` file, which is fine to skip. If codex.exe reappears in Task Manager right after you end it, tell me, because something is restarting it.\n\nneeds input: End all codex.exe and ChatGPT.exe in Task Manager > Details, delete the partial codex.zip, retry, and tell me how it goes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":370,"cache_read_input_tokens":149465,"output_tokens":830,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":381},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":370,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":830,"cache_read_input_tokens":149465,"cache_creation_input_tokens":370,"cache