{"parentUuid":"26da28ef-461b-4a4c-b320-0ba0fbfca1c9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqCcaZAr2etMU9hhhkcx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a new kind of error, and it's not a lock. Two things stand out:\n\n- **\"Availability status: Available when online\"** means `2024-25` is a **cloud placeholder**. The real files live in a cloud service, and the laptop only stores a pointer.\n- **\"The cloud file provider is not running\"** means the app behind that cloud folder, probably **OneDrive** or **Box Drive**, isn't running, so Windows can't fetch the files.\n\nThe good news: an online-only folder is **already stored in that cloud service**, not only on this laptop. Skipping it loses nothing.\n\nBefore you choose, I need to know where this came from, because I didn't expect a cloud folder inside any of the folders we're zipping:\n\n1. **Which operation was running?** The title says \"Copy Folder\", not \"Compress\". Were you copying something, or did this pop up during a zip? If so, which one?\n2. **Where does `2024-25` live?** If you're not sure, leave this box open and search File Explorer for `2024-25`, then tell me the path it shows.\n\nFor now, click **Skip** for this folder only, with \"Do this for all\" unchecked. Then answer the two questions above, and we'll confirm that `2024-25` actually exists in OneDrive or Box.\n\nneeds input: Tell me which copy or zip produced this error and the full path of the 2024-25 folder."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":391,"cache_read_input_tokens":151459,"output_tokens":800,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":361},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":391,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"i